<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka Jan-March '97 tea output 54.6 mln kg.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka Jan-March '97 tea output 54.6 mln kg.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's tea output in January- March 1997 fell 7.8 percent to 54.6 million kg from 59.2 million kg in the same 1996 period, the Central Bank said on Monday. Brokers said the crop shortfall was caused by drought over the winter months. Crops harvested during the current rainy season could make up for the shortfall, they said.</p>
</text>
